title: PierChatter
act: Arrival
scenario: The harbour dues
when: $act == Act.Arrival
---
// What the fishers say to each other on the pier. The game plays this group on a second dialogue runner, as captions,
// while the courier is near: it never stops the courier's own dialogue.
=> Maud: Twelve shillings. For a mooring ring and a hard look. #line:0f8973d
=> Joss: Let him say twelve to my face. #mood:angry #line:0fff164
=> Maud: The lamp was dark again last night. #line:0474001
=> Joss: Wind is backing. Rain by morning. #line:017a461
===

title: PierChatter
act: Wreck
scenario: Salvage
when: $act == Act.Wreck
---
=> Maud: Forty crates. I counted them twice. #line:04da0e9
=> Joss: Brandt counted them three times. #line:08ea30a
=> Maud: Odile would know what to do. <<if not $odile_here>> #line:08f1ae2
=> Joss: That passenger keeps looking at the lighthouse. #line:022d49c
===

title: PierChatter
act: HighTide
scenario: The vote
when: $act == Act.HighTide
---
=> Maud: No causeway today. We are an island again. #line:0b77fae
=> Joss: A vote. As if the sea cared who holds the key. #line:076d041
=> Maud: Three hands on the rope. That is all it takes. #line:00564d9
=> Joss: Did you see her? Odile is back! <<if $odile_here>> #line:0841922
===
